{
  "_comment": [
    "Baseline for tests/bundled-tool-packages.test.ts \u2014 the predecessor inventory that",
    "regeneration must not silently change. Taken from git history at the commit named",
    "in takenAt (the test verifies that commit exists, so a hand-edited provenance fails).",
    "",
    "WHEN TO RE-TAKE: only when a digest change is REVIEWED as intentional. Adding a",
    "package does NOT require re-taking this file \u2014 additions are asserted elsewhere and",
    "do not change an existing digest. A digest change must either be declared in",
    "intentionalReadmissions with a reason, or this baseline must be re-taken, which is a",
    "visible diff in review. That is the point: chrome-agent-platform-ne8u replaced a",
    "predecessor read from one author's worktree path with .catch(() => null), which made",
    "six assertions unreachable on every other machine.",
    "",
    "WHY NOT A ROLLING GIT WALK: measured over the last 300 commits touching the",
    "inventory, 9 transitions changed a shared package's digest, 12 added packages, and",
    "4 showed packages REMOVING and re-appearing (branch topology, not decisions). A",
    "rolling 'compare to the nearest differing ancestor' rule would need 13 historical",
    "adjudications, several of them merge artifacts, and would be vacuous on a clean",
    "checkout. A committed baseline with provenance is portable, has teeth, and makes the",
    "intentional-admission record a first-class artifact."
  ],
